**Language: Python.** A standalone CLI tool managed with [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/). Python is
the repo default for tools that aren't a better fit for Go (see the root `CLAUDE.md`).

## Requirements

- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (it manages the Python version and virtualenv).

## Commands

```bash
make sync       # uv sync — create .venv and install deps
make test       # uv run pytest
make lint       # ruff check + mypy (strict)
make fmt        # ruff format + ruff --fix
make run ARGS="Ada"
```

Or invoke the installed console script directly: `uv run {{ slug }} Ada`.

## Layout

```
src/{{ py_module }}/core.py        # pure logic — no argparse, the testable surface
src/{{ py_module }}/cli.py         # create_parser() + main(argv); wires logic to the CLI
src/{{ py_module }}/__main__.py    # `python -m {{ py_module }}`
tests/test_core.py / test_cli.py  # logic tests + parser/main tests
```

Logic lives in `core.py` and the CLI is a thin shell over it, so the bulk of behavior is tested
offline without touching argv or subprocesses.

## Updating from the template

```bash
copier update --trust   # pulls template improvements; answers are in .copier-answers.yml
```
